xval/area-trust/README.md gains the v2 readings of PREREGISTRATION-v2.md (signed off 9 November
2026): the v2 rule and what it changes (for N <= 6 the m clause is subsumed by the UNTRUSTED clause,
so v2 differs from v1 only in that one Untrusted station alone moves nothing); the rule selected by
"area_rule": "v2" in the stations document (absent: v1, bytes unchanged) and by an explicit
argument on the live path; T2's added check read as "raises an area alert, DEGRADED or worse", a
disclosed reading of a word that conflicts with the rule's order; T1 and T5 on the seven committed
replays; the T4 fortnight (the first 14 consecutive days from 20 January 2025 with every 3-hour Kp
<= 4.000), selected by script and committed before any observation file is fetched; reading 10 anew,
reading 9, and B8 reading 8 for the navigation file; stop and ask if a file cannot be fetched; T3
re-run as written, runs one after another.

xval/area-trust/oracle_v2.py is oracle.py with the v2 m clause, reading the area_rule field. On the
committed documents without the field it writes v1's bytes exactly (both boundary documents, replays
4101 and 4107). oracle.py is not changed.
